PREAMBLE

This repository contains original research software, models, data, and
documentation developed by W. T. Campagna as part of the AURA-MPC project.
AURA-MPC integrates multi-fidelity atmospheric radiation simulation with
model predictive control for photovoltaic systems.

This license exists because the work here is live, ongoing academic research.
The author wants it to be openly readable and useful to the research community
while retaining control over commercial use, redistribution, and misuse as
AI/ML training material. The terms below are written to be clear and direct —
not to create legal barriers, but to protect the integrity of the research and
the ability of the author to continue developing it.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

SECTION 1 — PERMITTED USES (Academic and Personal)

You are permitted to:

  1.1  Read, download, and run the code, data, and documentation in this
       repository for personal study or non-commercial academic research.

  1.2  Reference and reproduce small excerpts (e.g., equations, algorithms,
       configuration snippets) in academic publications, theses, reports, or
       presentations, provided you include a proper citation as described in
       Section 3 and the "How to Cite" section at the end of this file.

  1.3  Build on this work privately for academic research purposes, subject
       to the conditions in Section 5 (share-back).

